1
00:00:27,260 --> 00:00:28,650
(THE YARNS)

2
00:01:12,952 --> 00:01:14,632
Lan, the victim couldn't breathe on his own.

3
00:01:16,582 --> 00:01:19,440
His airways were blocked until he suffocated.

4
00:01:19,805 --> 00:01:22,120
You must close this case before the election.

5
00:01:22,521 --> 00:01:27,344
Sky is the orphan I adopted.

6
00:01:27,580 --> 00:01:29,699
Yes, it's really you. I remember now.

7
00:01:29,931 --> 00:01:33,321
That day at the boxing camp,
you asked me to call Nop to come see you.

8
00:01:33,462 --> 00:01:34,952
Then you both disappeared for the whole night.

9
00:01:35,036 --> 00:01:36,144
When I saw him again, he was already a corpse.

10
00:01:36,274 --> 00:01:39,314
Do you know that woman's name and where she lives?

11
00:01:39,367 --> 00:01:41,927
I heard she calls herself

12
00:01:42,529 --> 00:01:43,817
Fah

13
00:01:44,857 --> 00:01:46,110
I'm so excited.

14
00:01:46,384 --> 00:01:48,822
Sky has a twin sister who looks just like Sky.

15
00:01:49,104 --> 00:01:52,556
And Sky has a twin sister named Fah.

16
00:01:52,952 --> 00:01:55,489
S-K-Y means Fah.

17
00:02:33,523 --> 00:02:34,506
Excuse me

18
00:02:51,028 --> 00:02:54,350
Have you ever seen this man in the picture before?

19
00:02:58,933 --> 00:02:59,813
Never

20
00:03:03,280 --> 00:03:04,129
Thank you

21
00:03:42,293 --> 00:03:43,078
Look

22
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:46,384
If Sky wasn't the one fighting the victim

23
00:03:46,651 --> 00:03:48,826
Then it had to be someone who shares her DNA.

24
00:03:49,356 --> 00:03:51,356
They look so alike, it's like they're the same person.

25
00:03:51,897 --> 00:03:54,780
Who else could it be if not identical twins?

26
00:03:55,348 --> 00:03:57,161
Identical twins. From the same egg

27
00:03:58,182 --> 00:04:00,422
So Sky really has a twin.

28
00:04:00,758 --> 00:04:02,514
And Miss Sookwan doesn't even know about it.

29
00:04:03,908 --> 00:04:06,091
In that case, does the killer know they have a twin?

30
00:04:06,533 --> 00:04:08,380
I'm not sure either.

31
00:04:09,641 --> 00:04:11,398
If neither of them knows

32
00:04:11,847 --> 00:04:15,580
Is it just a coincidence their names are so similar?

33
00:04:16,251 --> 00:04:18,468
Sky and Fah. Fah and Sky.

34
00:04:19,146 --> 00:04:20,853
It's possible, Sergeant.

35
00:04:21,280 --> 00:04:24,266
I've seen documentaries on YouTube about twins.

36
00:04:24,750 --> 00:04:28,651
Some twins are separated at birth and never even know they have a sibling.

37
00:04:29,104 --> 00:04:32,114
But strange coincidences still happen, like

38
00:04:32,415 --> 00:04:33,763
naming their dogs the same name.

39
00:04:34,388 --> 00:04:34,979
Ah

40
00:04:35,455 --> 00:04:36,320
And

41
00:04:36,514 --> 00:04:38,609
Did that boxer say anything else about Fah, Inspector?

42
00:04:42,563 --> 00:04:43,880
At first, you said

43
00:04:44,380 --> 00:04:47,653
Nopphachai didn't want to go with her.
So why'd he suddenly agree?

44
00:04:47,908 --> 00:04:50,784
That woman, Fah threatened him.

45
00:04:51,443 --> 00:04:55,310
Threatened? A woman threatened a boxer? With what?

46
00:04:55,946 --> 00:04:57,542
She said something about killer genes.

47
00:04:59,139 --> 00:05:00,179
You have to go with me.

48
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:03,539
If you don't, I'll expose the fact that you have the killer genes.

49
00:05:04,200 --> 00:05:06,643
But your dad bought someone else's genes and faked them for you.

50
00:05:08,175 --> 00:05:10,354
How do you know? What proof do you have?

51
00:05:11,146 --> 00:05:13,573
You’ll find out—if you don’t come with me.

52
00:05:14,011 --> 00:05:18,137
Tomorrow, the news will spread everywhere.
A rising star boxer with the killer genes.

53
00:05:18,834 --> 00:05:23,085
And worse—you and your dad will be arrested for buying someone else’s genes.

54
00:05:23,786 --> 00:05:26,247
When Nop died, I went straight to his dad.

55
00:05:26,727 --> 00:05:29,192
But his dad told me not to say a word to anyone.

56
00:05:36,830 --> 00:05:37,440
So

57
00:05:37,801 --> 00:05:40,110
The first victim had the killer genes.

58
00:05:40,480 --> 00:05:42,426
So the father had to cover it up.

59
00:05:43,040 --> 00:05:45,977
As for the part about meeting that woman named Fah
he couldn’t talk about it.

60
00:05:47,146 --> 00:05:48,914
If he'd told us from the start

61
00:05:49,870 --> 00:05:52,156
We could've sketched the suspect's face.

62
00:05:52,438 --> 00:05:54,019
And we might've caught them in time.

63
00:05:54,601 --> 00:05:56,300
Rapee probably wouldn't have... Sergeant.

64
00:05:57,733 --> 00:06:00,548
It's not that simple.

65
00:06:01,257 --> 00:06:02,560
Don't forget that at the start

66
00:06:03,123 --> 00:06:05,908
We had no leads before we found Sky.

67
00:06:06,354 --> 00:06:08,780
So, I’ll assign the unit to search the area.

68
00:06:09,401 --> 00:06:11,436
Look for anyone who resembles Sky.

69
00:06:15,222 --> 00:06:15,904
An

70
00:06:16,643 --> 00:06:22,120
Would you mind helping us test
for the killer genes in every corpse?

71
00:06:22,438 --> 00:06:23,154
Huh?

72
00:06:24,070 --> 00:06:27,710
Lan wants me to check for
the killer’s genesin all the bodies?

73
00:06:28,095 --> 00:06:31,097
Yes, we want to prove something.

74
00:06:32,796 --> 00:06:36,179
Even... Rapeephan too?

75
00:06:39,200 --> 00:06:40,251
What exactly is Lan trying to prove?

76
00:06:41,320 --> 00:06:42,045
Can you do it?

77
00:06:42,739 --> 00:06:43,626
I can

78
00:06:43,939 --> 00:06:47,371
All the bodies were impounded in the institute’s freezer.

79
00:06:50,800 --> 00:06:52,826
Doctor, you have my permission to run the test.

80
00:06:55,577 --> 00:06:56,228
An

81
00:06:57,180 --> 00:06:58,308
Can you do it as soon as you can?

82
00:06:59,234 --> 00:06:59,980
Okay

83
00:07:08,895 --> 00:07:09,805
Yes, Miss Sookwan.

84
00:07:17,177 --> 00:07:19,108
When did Sky knit this piece of yarn?

85
00:07:19,843 --> 00:07:22,636
I guess she did it after she got home.

86
00:07:23,299 --> 00:07:27,500
Inspector, do you remember when we picked up Sky
and she said she had to hurry home to knit?

87
00:07:27,958 --> 00:07:28,624
I remember.

88
00:07:29,173 --> 00:07:32,106
But I thought Sky had gone back to regular knitting.

89
00:07:32,655 --> 00:07:35,382
I felt the same way

90
00:07:35,440 --> 00:07:37,737
Until I found this.

91
00:08:25,676 --> 00:08:28,689
Sky kept knitting — and hiding it.

92
00:08:29,862 --> 00:08:33,527
Are you saying Sky knew what was happening… and saw it?

93
00:08:33,904 --> 00:08:35,767
I'm not sure either.

94
00:08:36,030 --> 00:08:39,245
At first, I thought Sky had gone out,

95
00:08:39,398 --> 00:08:42,925
got caught in something, then came back to knit.
But this time, she was at the prison.

96
00:08:43,695 --> 00:08:47,980
Just like when the Venerable Monk passed away
Sky was with me.

97
00:08:48,784 --> 00:08:52,571
When Rapeephan's death was caught on CCTV...

98
00:08:53,089 --> 00:08:56,217
Miss Sookwan, who did you pick up from school that day?

99
00:08:57,680 --> 00:08:58,826
Sky.

100
00:08:59,630 --> 00:09:01,740
I met her there.

101
00:09:02,506 --> 00:09:06,453
So… are you saying Sky actually knew where it would happen?

102
00:09:08,876 --> 00:09:09,836
How would she know?

103
00:09:15,192 --> 00:09:17,051
Everyone, please don’t look at me like that.

104
00:09:17,497 --> 00:09:20,518
This is beyond what science can explain.

105
00:09:20,998 --> 00:09:22,716
But it's very possible.

106
00:09:22,963 --> 00:09:27,120
That Sky’s episodes happen before each murder.

107
00:09:27,455 --> 00:09:28,834
I think we need to keep an eye on her.

108
00:09:29,375 --> 00:09:30,819
Watch for when she has another episode.

109
00:09:31,180 --> 00:09:33,474
And most importantly, find out who the killer will target next.

110
00:09:33,840 --> 00:09:35,142
Before Sky had her episode.

111
00:09:35,238 --> 00:09:39,474
But we still haven’t solved
the riddle of Grandpa Som’s Treasure.

112
00:10:12,057 --> 00:10:13,596
This is our next target.

113
00:10:14,380 --> 00:10:16,095
Pick someone easy.

114
00:10:17,798 --> 00:10:18,537
Fah

115
00:10:19,180 --> 00:10:20,864
Are you sure you really want to keep going?

116
00:10:21,737 --> 00:10:23,405
You almost got caught last time, remember?

117
00:10:24,129 --> 00:10:24,906
Why?

118
00:10:25,725 --> 00:10:27,847
- You scared now?
- Yeah.

119
00:10:28,266 --> 00:10:29,478
I admit it. I’m scared.

120
00:10:30,038 --> 00:10:30,800
And now

121
00:10:31,222 --> 00:10:32,803
The cops know your face.

122
00:10:33,219 --> 00:10:34,280
Because of your twin.

123
00:10:34,590 --> 00:10:36,464
I’m not scared.
Why the hell would you be

124
00:10:36,651 --> 00:10:37,782
if I’m the one getting caught?

125
00:10:37,880 --> 00:10:39,070
I’ll take all the blame. On my own.

126
00:10:40,982 --> 00:10:41,729
Lily

127
00:10:42,460 --> 00:10:44,636
Just go get me the list of people who secretly bought genes.

128
00:10:44,680 --> 00:10:47,535
From the civil registry where you work.
I only need one more name.

129
00:10:47,775 --> 00:10:48,769
Then you're done.

130
00:10:50,822 --> 00:10:51,580
As for Keng

131
00:10:52,506 --> 00:10:54,948
Just bring that person to me like you always do.

132
00:10:56,650 --> 00:10:57,062
But

133
00:10:57,080 --> 00:10:58,952
if you change your mind and back out,
I’ll do it myself.

134
00:11:01,683 --> 00:11:03,093
It's not like that, Fah.

135
00:11:03,520 --> 00:11:06,080
I’m not leaving you. We grew up together.

136
00:11:06,499 --> 00:11:08,662
I know someone like you wouldn’t dump this on us.

137
00:11:09,120 --> 00:11:11,782
But we’re both really worried about you, Fah.

138
00:11:12,281 --> 00:11:13,040
Yeah.

139
00:11:13,619 --> 00:11:15,729
Isn’t there a better way?

140
00:11:16,960 --> 00:11:17,767
A better way?

141
00:11:18,316 --> 00:11:20,114
You see those guys screaming in protest?

142
00:11:20,723 --> 00:11:22,335
I’ve heard them shouting since I was born.

143
00:11:22,670 --> 00:11:24,864
Even now, nothing’s gotten any better.

144
00:11:25,268 --> 00:11:27,154
Scream all you want — loud enough to reach Mars

145
00:11:27,184 --> 00:11:28,308
No one’s listening to you.

146
00:11:29,447 --> 00:11:31,276
Because we’re the ones at the bottom of society.

147
00:11:33,508 --> 00:11:34,994
That’s why I chose the quiet way.

148
00:11:35,462 --> 00:11:38,297
A silence that screams louder than anyone could imagine.

149
00:11:39,032 --> 00:11:40,240
But if you get caught

150
00:11:40,780 --> 00:11:41,946
You’re dead for sure, Fah.

151
00:11:42,228 --> 00:11:44,761
Then what’s the difference between living like this and being dead?

152
00:11:51,127 --> 00:11:54,304
Don’t you remember?
Every job you applied for nearly bled you dry.

153
00:11:54,845 --> 00:11:56,918
Once people find out we have those killer genes

154
00:11:57,508 --> 00:12:00,640
They treat us like we’re infected
like we’re contagious.

155
00:12:01,939 --> 00:12:02,800
They shut us out.

156
00:12:03,241 --> 00:12:04,335
They kill our dreams

157
00:12:04,678 --> 00:12:06,540
cut us off from everything we should’ve had.

158
00:12:09,245 --> 00:12:10,125
As for Keng

159
00:12:10,834 --> 00:12:11,828
You wanted to be a cop.

160
00:12:12,320 --> 00:12:13,180
I wanted to be a doctor.

161
00:12:14,380 --> 00:12:16,880
But isn’t it those damn laws that stopped us?

162
00:12:19,093 --> 00:12:20,380
And the truth is

163
00:12:20,990 --> 00:12:23,676
Neither of us even have those killer genes.

164
00:12:24,548 --> 00:12:26,891
But your dad, my grandma

165
00:12:27,782 --> 00:12:29,295
They sold those genes to someone else.

166
00:12:30,403 --> 00:12:32,278
As if being born poor wasn’t punishment enough.

167
00:12:32,674 --> 00:12:34,365
We’ve still got to take the fall for what others did.

168
00:12:36,403 --> 00:12:39,382
Judged a killer before we could even speak.

169
00:12:40,163 --> 00:12:40,944
And you

170
00:12:42,354 --> 00:12:48,015
You forget how your dad used to slap you around?
Forget what it felt like getting stomped under his boot?

171
00:12:48,674 --> 00:12:51,748
You both forgot what we’ve been through?

172
00:12:57,001 --> 00:12:58,243
And even if you pull this off

173
00:12:59,370 --> 00:13:01,417
You think we can actually take that law down?

174
00:13:02,041 --> 00:13:02,857
I don’t know.

175
00:13:03,650 --> 00:13:05,805
All I know is, that’ll let me get revenge for my mum.

176
00:13:07,817 --> 00:13:08,925
That bastard.

177
00:13:09,580 --> 00:13:11,337
I’ll open the gates of hell for him myself.

178
00:13:28,780 --> 00:13:30,601
All the victims’ DNA results are in.

179
00:13:32,788 --> 00:13:34,567
Every single one had the killer genes.

180
00:13:34,952 --> 00:13:38,822
Except those killed outside the plan.
Those cases involved forgery and corruption.

181
00:13:39,135 --> 00:13:41,249
Meaning the victim didn’t actually have the killer genes.

182
00:13:42,529 --> 00:13:43,424
Faked genes.

183
00:13:43,946 --> 00:13:48,099
Yes, Sergeant. According to official records,
not all victims had the genes.

184
00:13:48,739 --> 00:13:50,415
But when I rechecked—just like the Inspector asked me to

185
00:13:50,792 --> 00:13:52,434
I found that all of them did have the killer genes.

186
00:13:52,956 --> 00:13:54,118
Yeah, I’ve heard about that before.

187
00:13:54,739 --> 00:14:00,274
But I’ve never seen a real case.
Because the legal penalty is harsh, for both buyer and seller.

188
00:14:00,880 --> 00:14:02,457
But that’s not the only issue, Lan.

189
00:14:03,222 --> 00:14:06,419
Now it turns out, people without the killer gene

190
00:14:06,693 --> 00:14:09,737
are the ones killing those who have it.

191
00:14:10,929 --> 00:14:13,729
Is the killer trying to send a message?

192
00:14:14,148 --> 00:14:15,005
Inspector.

193
00:14:17,043 --> 00:14:19,013
May I see Rapeephan’s results?

194
00:14:52,384 --> 00:14:55,180
I'm exhausted from dealing with other people’s kids all day.

195
00:14:55,394 --> 00:14:57,660
When will we finally have a kid of our own?

196
00:15:00,830 --> 00:15:01,946
We’ve talked about this so many times.

197
00:15:02,540 --> 00:15:06,346
That we’re not having kids.
Why not, love? Scared of losing your figure?

198
00:15:06,560 --> 00:15:08,666
It’s okay, love. Even if you’re not pretty.

199
00:15:08,834 --> 00:15:09,897
I’ll still love you just the same.

200
00:15:10,179 --> 00:15:11,980
I said no — and I mean it.

201
00:15:12,579 --> 00:15:13,546
If you really want one

202
00:15:13,916 --> 00:15:14,979
Then go have one with someone else.

203
00:15:17,036 --> 00:15:20,247
Now I get why Rapeephan didn’t want to have kids.

204
00:15:23,394 --> 00:15:28,499
But don’t worry. If Rapeephan really was involved in gene trading corruption

205
00:15:28,860 --> 00:15:31,386
I’d want to know the truth about the whole operation too.

206
00:15:32,247 --> 00:15:36,049
Then let’s arrest everyone responsible.
You’re right, Sergeant.

207
00:15:36,784 --> 00:15:44,095
Catching the culprit matters too, Sergeant.
But I think we should use this opportunity to lure the killer out.

208
00:15:44,700 --> 00:15:46,217
I honestly wonder

209
00:15:46,680 --> 00:15:49,462
How did the murderer know who was buying and selling genes?

210
00:15:49,828 --> 00:15:51,013
That's suspicious.

211
00:15:51,580 --> 00:15:54,030
But what we really need to watch out for, Inspector

212
00:15:54,948 --> 00:15:56,441
is letting this leak.

213
00:15:56,731 --> 00:15:58,403
Because the first person who got publicly dragged was

214
00:15:59,489 --> 00:16:00,377
the Inspector’s father.

215
00:16:03,504 --> 00:16:04,312
But

216
00:16:04,918 --> 00:16:06,693
Dr. Chonlathorn has nothing to do with this.

217
00:16:07,280 --> 00:16:08,933
He just drafted the law.

218
00:16:09,512 --> 00:16:11,028
That’s where the corruption started.

219
00:16:12,563 --> 00:16:14,598
No one wants to have killer genes.

220
00:16:15,009 --> 00:16:19,302
And no one wants to have their freedom taken away.

221
00:16:23,588 --> 00:16:24,365
Yes

222
00:16:25,405 --> 00:16:26,243
Exactly

223
00:16:27,440 --> 00:16:28,232
Yes, that's right.

224
00:16:29,268 --> 00:16:31,474
This is what the killer’s been trying to say all along.

225
00:16:33,280 --> 00:16:34,430
It matches exactly with this book.

226
00:16:35,763 --> 00:16:38,895
Medical Science and the Barriers to Humanity.

227
00:16:40,598 --> 00:16:41,363
Whoa.

228
00:16:42,186 --> 00:16:42,963
That’s genius.

229
00:16:43,702 --> 00:16:45,904
So what will Fah do next?

230
00:16:46,685 --> 00:16:48,133
Is she really planning to kill all ten?

231
00:16:49,520 --> 00:16:50,339
So what?

232
00:16:53,672 --> 00:16:55,234
We need to go back to the root of all this.

233
00:16:57,371 --> 00:16:59,480
(Mr. Pakin Phiamlam-arun, Director of the Office)

234
00:17:04,624 --> 00:17:05,474
Come in.

235
00:17:06,537 --> 00:17:08,880
Hello, I’m Police Lieutenant Colonel Pilanthorn Traikanon.

236
00:17:09,360 --> 00:17:12,925
I’m here to bring you in to give a statement
at the Special Investigation Unit.

237
00:17:14,205 --> 00:17:14,925
What?

238
00:17:15,782 --> 00:17:19,668
I don’t understand have I done something wrong?

239
00:17:20,834 --> 00:17:25,089
You’re a suspect in a case
involving the forging of genetic data.

240
00:17:27,024 --> 00:17:32,331
I didn’t do anything,
and I don’t know a thing about forged documents.

241
00:17:33,447 --> 00:17:34,331
I didn’t forge anything.

242
00:17:34,780 --> 00:17:37,714
If you didn’t, that’s fine.
We just want to have a conversation.

243
00:17:41,089 --> 00:17:41,916
Alright.

244
00:17:43,912 --> 00:17:45,203
But if I’ve done nothing wrong

245
00:17:46,377 --> 00:17:47,638
I’ll definitely sue you back.

246
00:17:48,598 --> 00:17:49,440
Please come with us.

247
00:17:56,266 --> 00:17:57,386
What is this?

248
00:17:58,514 --> 00:18:00,308
The police are gathering evidence of corruption.

249
00:18:00,792 --> 00:18:03,020
Without even asking for my permission?

250
00:18:03,580 --> 00:18:06,624
You have no right to take anything from this place.

251
00:18:07,969 --> 00:18:10,780
I’ll call Dr Chonlathorn.
I’ve already informed him, sir.

252
00:18:12,788 --> 00:18:13,451
Take him.

253
00:18:14,380 --> 00:18:16,080
Yes, sir. Let’s go.

254
00:18:16,655 --> 00:18:17,836
Don't touch me.

255
00:18:18,346 --> 00:18:19,180
Let go of me.

256
00:18:28,640 --> 00:18:30,293
What you said just now, Inspector.

257
00:18:30,920 --> 00:18:31,771
What does that mean?

258
00:18:32,792 --> 00:18:34,403
I honestly don’t know what any of this is about.

259
00:18:35,622 --> 00:18:37,779
Let me be clear I don’t know anything.

260
00:18:38,660 --> 00:18:39,916
There’s been a complaint.

261
00:18:41,047 --> 00:18:43,523
About a black market for killer genes.

262
00:18:44,742 --> 00:18:47,760
Director, have you heard anything about this?

263
00:18:48,906 --> 00:18:51,158
I told you — never.

264
00:18:52,933 --> 00:18:55,451
Where did you even hear these rumors, Inspector?

265
00:18:55,969 --> 00:18:59,036
The person who filed the complaint seems pretty credible.

266
00:19:00,891 --> 00:19:11,504
You think that person is more credible than me?
I’m the Director of the Office of Criminal Records!

267
00:19:13,493 --> 00:19:16,689
Director, have you ever heard the phrase,
“The dead don’t lie”?

268
00:19:17,653 --> 00:19:18,506
Hmm

269
00:19:20,796 --> 00:19:21,424
Here.

270
00:19:21,881 --> 00:19:25,630
Autopsy results for all the victims in the serial murder case.

271
00:19:26,163 --> 00:19:30,240
They all had the murder gene.
But according to the civil registry

272
00:19:30,830 --> 00:19:31,817
It says they didn’t.

273
00:19:32,838 --> 00:19:34,601
And the person who signed off on those documents.

274
00:19:35,980 --> 00:19:36,967
Was you.

275
00:19:40,617 --> 00:19:41,611
I

276
00:19:42,998 --> 00:19:43,843
I didn’t know anything about it.

277
00:19:44,278 --> 00:19:45,531
Whatever documents they handed me

278
00:19:45,912 --> 00:19:47,120
I just signed them.

279
00:19:47,794 --> 00:19:50,720
- Then if you’ll excuse me...
- Hold on.

280
00:19:52,247 --> 00:19:54,472
If there’s anything else you want to know, Inspector

281
00:19:54,750 --> 00:19:56,297
I’ll have my lawyer contact you.

282
00:19:57,680 --> 00:19:59,980
- That’s it.
- Just hear me out first, Mr Pakin.

283
00:20:01,009 --> 00:20:03,245
The list of the next victims

284
00:20:04,548 --> 00:20:05,508
is in your hands.

285
00:20:06,693 --> 00:20:10,095
If you hand over the list of everyone involved in the gene trade

286
00:20:11,192 --> 00:20:13,032
I’ll treat you as a cooperating witness.

287
00:20:14,849 --> 00:20:16,780
That’d be way easier than hiring a lawyer, don’t you think?

288
00:20:23,560 --> 00:20:24,285
Take him.

289
00:20:25,180 --> 00:20:26,731
Yes, sir. Let’s go.

290
00:20:35,081 --> 00:20:39,131
By now, they’ve probably figured out the gene trade and how it was used to falsify records.

291
00:20:39,660 --> 00:20:41,527
Everything’s going exactly according to the plan I laid out.

292
00:20:43,238 --> 00:20:44,190
Thanks to Man

293
00:20:44,605 --> 00:20:47,234
He helped put on a show to throw
off the cops they were onto this.

294
00:20:47,767 --> 00:20:48,944
That was nothing.

295
00:20:51,390 --> 00:20:52,514
Easy as hell, man.

296
00:20:53,024 --> 00:20:54,605
I just said exactly what you told me to.

297
00:20:55,180 --> 00:20:58,186
Besides, Nop really did fake his killer gene.

298
00:20:58,979 --> 00:21:00,041
His dad told me himself.

299
00:21:01,420 --> 00:21:02,133
Yeah

300
00:21:02,670 --> 00:21:05,466
Then how’d you know that cop would come around here?

301
00:21:09,074 --> 00:21:10,300
Hello, Grandma.

302
00:21:10,662 --> 00:21:14,041
I’m a relative of Grandma Duangjai — she used to rent from you.

303
00:21:14,080 --> 00:21:15,240
She used to run a laundry shop.

304
00:21:15,580 --> 00:21:16,655
Do you remember?

305
00:21:16,876 --> 00:21:18,556
Oh, I remember!

306
00:21:18,640 --> 00:21:19,859
I remember it clearly.

307
00:21:20,060 --> 00:21:23,123
Grandma Duangjai has gone quiet lately.
How has she been, dear?

308
00:21:23,432 --> 00:21:26,560
She’s doing well. She’s staying with me now.

309
00:21:26,662 --> 00:21:30,777
Oh — she sent this curry for you. Braised pork belly with cowa leaves.

310
00:21:31,916 --> 00:21:33,024
Wow!

311
00:21:33,478 --> 00:21:37,055
That smell coming through
the bag definitely her cooking.

312
00:21:37,131 --> 00:21:38,662
I’d recognize it anywhere, dear.

313
00:21:39,070 --> 00:21:41,219
So where’s Grandma Duangjai staying now?

314
00:21:41,680 --> 00:21:43,958
Just in case I want to go visit her.

315
00:21:48,106 --> 00:21:50,415
Fah, is this all your plan?

316
00:21:52,312 --> 00:21:53,386
I don’t get it.

317
00:21:54,445 --> 00:21:58,514
Why are you even doing this?
You don’t need to know. When this is over

318
00:21:59,120 --> 00:22:02,224
Your girlfriend Lily will be the one who benefits.
That’s all you need to know.

319
00:22:03,531 --> 00:22:04,609
You are so full of it.

320
00:22:09,320 --> 00:22:10,194
Hello.

321
00:22:10,979 --> 00:22:13,356
Oh, about the Director? I haven’t heard anything yet.

322
00:22:13,740 --> 00:22:14,544
Really?

323
00:22:14,975 --> 00:22:15,923
Yes, Waew.

324
00:22:16,034 --> 00:22:17,245
We’ll talk later, okay?

325
00:22:17,580 --> 00:22:18,632
Yes. Thank you.

326
00:22:20,674 --> 00:22:21,497
What’s up?

327
00:22:22,030 --> 00:22:25,180
That bastard director got away.
The cops just let him walk right out.

328
00:22:25,390 --> 00:22:26,380
Shit.

329
00:22:27,394 --> 00:22:28,780
What's next then?

330
00:22:41,680 --> 00:22:44,335
Oh, Sky! Here to see the Inspector?

331
00:22:45,188 --> 00:22:49,318
- Yes, Sky came to see the lieutenant.
- The police lieutenant hasn't arrived yet.

332
00:22:49,748 --> 00:22:52,312
Do you want to wait upstairs?
I'll have Bee take you.

333
00:22:53,260 --> 00:22:54,034
Thank you.

334
00:22:59,680 --> 00:23:00,948
Come on in, Sky.

335
00:23:02,400 --> 00:23:04,171
Sky, just have a seat over there.

336
00:23:14,438 --> 00:23:15,337
I’ll head out first.

337
00:23:34,240 --> 00:23:35,040
Thank you

338
00:23:42,289 --> 00:23:43,417
Hello, Inspector.

339
00:23:44,137 --> 00:23:45,428
Hello, Sky

340
00:23:45,885 --> 00:23:46,640
Hello.

341
00:23:46,815 --> 00:23:49,794
My name is Sky. Sky means the space above the Earth.

342
00:23:50,533 --> 00:23:51,580
I already know.

343
00:23:51,954 --> 00:23:53,203
You know, you can say something else when greeting someone.

344
00:23:53,241 --> 00:23:54,819
Don't you get bored saying the same thing every day?

345
00:23:55,680 --> 00:23:56,670
Um, Inspector.

346
00:23:56,975 --> 00:23:58,460
I'm gonna go buy coffee.

347
00:23:58,720 --> 00:24:00,072
Would you like anything, Inspector?

348
00:24:00,327 --> 00:24:01,554
No, thanks. You go ahead.

349
00:24:03,683 --> 00:24:05,272
You came back downstairs quickly, Sky.

350
00:24:05,714 --> 00:24:07,561
Didn't you just go up with Bee?

351
00:24:08,710 --> 00:24:10,533
I didn't go upstairs

352
00:24:10,689 --> 00:24:13,127
I just got here with the officer.

353
00:24:15,485 --> 00:24:16,407
Wait, what do you mean?

354
00:24:16,735 --> 00:24:19,760
Did you just take Sky up to my office?

355
00:24:20,156 --> 00:24:21,074
Yes.

356
00:24:21,668 --> 00:24:24,320
But when did Sky change clothes? That was so fast.

357
00:24:25,333 --> 00:24:26,160
Everyone, listen up,

358
00:24:26,205 --> 00:24:28,259
Lock down the office. No one gets in or out.

359
00:24:28,499 --> 00:24:29,207
Yes, sir.

360
00:24:32,796 --> 00:24:37,558
All entrances and exits to the police building are now closed.
No one enters or leaves until further notice.

361
00:24:48,217 --> 00:24:50,080
Sky, wait for me here.

362
00:24:50,720 --> 00:24:51,920
Sky’s upstairs.

363
00:24:53,089 --> 00:24:56,895
Sky, listen stay right here. Don't move, understand?

364
00:24:59,120 --> 00:25:00,480
Sky's twin is upstairs.

365
00:25:04,780 --> 00:25:06,354
Sky's twin is upstairs.

366
00:25:07,893 --> 00:25:09,504
Sky's twin is upstairs.

367
00:25:18,944 --> 00:25:19,760
Woah.

368
00:27:49,131 --> 00:27:49,794
Stop!

369
00:27:49,843 --> 00:27:50,680
Don't move!

370
00:27:51,139 --> 00:27:53,240
- Officer, this is Sky!
- Quiet!

371
00:27:53,520 --> 00:27:55,908
Face the wall! Face the wall!

372
00:27:57,188 --> 00:27:59,748
Sergeant, I found Fah. Cancel the order.

373
00:28:01,356 --> 00:28:02,285
Face the wall!

374
00:28:02,600 --> 00:28:03,352
Yes.

375
00:28:04,472 --> 00:28:08,280
- Ouch! Officer. That hurts! Let go of me!
- Stop struggling!

376
00:28:08,590 --> 00:28:11,432
- This is Sky, Officer.
- Don't move.

377
00:28:11,520 --> 00:28:12,670
Let Sky go.

378
00:28:13,116 --> 00:28:14,960
- Yes, Inspector.
- Take her.

379
00:28:17,489 --> 00:28:19,241
Officer, please let go.

380
00:28:19,417 --> 00:28:20,613
Let go, you're hurting Sky.

381
00:28:20,651 --> 00:28:22,407
Officer, I'm Sky!

382
00:28:22,468 --> 00:28:24,072
I'm Sky, Officer.

383
00:28:26,712 --> 00:28:29,680
Let go, Officer this is Sky.

384
00:28:32,380 --> 00:28:33,108
Sky!

385
00:28:33,927 --> 00:28:35,920
Yes, it's really me Sky.

386
00:28:36,468 --> 00:28:40,480
Sky means the space above the Earth.
I'm not the twin.

387
00:28:42,582 --> 00:28:44,933
Let go! Just let go!

388
00:28:49,074 --> 00:28:50,293
What's going on, Sky?

389
00:28:51,283 --> 00:28:52,400
How did you get here?

390
00:28:52,895 --> 00:28:57,497
Why are you wearing Fah’s shirt?
Which question do you want me to answer first?

391
00:29:00,200 --> 00:29:01,714
How did you get here, Sky?

392
00:29:04,270 --> 00:29:05,870
Sky's twin is upstairs.

393
00:29:06,540 --> 00:29:08,270
Sky's twin is upstairs.

394
00:29:09,680 --> 00:29:11,542
Officer told Sky to wait here.

395
00:29:12,200 --> 00:29:13,580
What happened, Ek?

396
00:29:13,916 --> 00:29:18,200
Why aren't people allowed to enter or leave the building?
I don't know either, but it looks serious.

397
00:29:19,432 --> 00:29:21,520
That's what I thought too.

398
00:29:21,923 --> 00:29:23,405
We should head back to the room.

399
00:29:23,820 --> 00:29:26,822
Oh, the elevator’s here. Come on, hurry.

400
00:29:26,910 --> 00:29:28,346
Sky can't go in there.

401
00:29:28,499 --> 00:29:30,636
Officer told Sky to wait downstairs.

402
00:30:07,074 --> 00:30:07,920
Oh.

403
00:30:24,068 --> 00:30:25,238
Where’s that cop?

404
00:30:28,350 --> 00:30:30,293
He's...He's in this building.

405
00:30:31,180 --> 00:30:32,400
He's coming up, isn't he?

406
00:30:34,689 --> 00:30:35,520
Right?

407
00:30:39,832 --> 00:30:40,680
Good

408
00:30:41,234 --> 00:30:43,539
It's time for Muta to help Munin.

409
00:30:48,520 --> 00:30:49,360
Wow

410
00:30:50,007 --> 00:30:51,249
It fits perfectly.

411
00:30:53,880 --> 00:30:55,142
When I wore it, it was a bit loose.

412
00:30:56,240 --> 00:30:57,580
I guess I've been starving more than you, huh?

413
00:31:07,234 --> 00:31:08,739
Give this to your Officer.

414
00:31:32,434 --> 00:31:33,192
Bye

415
00:31:33,880 --> 00:31:34,680
Sky

416
00:31:44,335 --> 00:31:45,699
Sky

417
00:31:57,360 --> 00:32:00,327
My twin told me to give this to Officer.

418
00:32:08,720 --> 00:32:09,200
Sergeant.

419
00:32:09,920 --> 00:32:12,560
Check every CCTV camera.
I'll handle things here.

420
00:32:12,891 --> 00:32:13,840
Yes, Inspector.

421
00:32:18,380 --> 00:32:19,352
Are you hurt, Sky?

422
00:32:20,899 --> 00:32:21,744
Yes, it hurts.

423
00:32:22,910 --> 00:32:24,297
But Sky can handle it.

424
00:32:24,727 --> 00:32:25,584
I'm really sorry.

425
00:32:25,668 --> 00:32:28,520
I think Fah was trying to speak like Sky.

426
00:32:28,628 --> 00:32:30,247
Acting like Sky to trick me.

427
00:32:31,992 --> 00:32:33,447
I'm sorry. I'm really sorry.

428
00:32:33,931 --> 00:32:35,043
It's okay.

429
00:32:35,706 --> 00:32:38,735
Even Sky can't tell me apart from my twin.

430
00:32:39,752 --> 00:32:42,918
Oh, but my twin sister is thinner than Sky.

431
00:32:43,478 --> 00:32:45,459
She said she doesn't eat much.

432
00:33:28,040 --> 00:33:31,268
What did the killer want here? Did she take anything?

433
00:33:32,091 --> 00:33:33,710
I think Fah came to check the documents.

434
00:33:34,396 --> 00:33:36,280
To see if the victims she killed really had the killer genes.

435
00:33:36,887 --> 00:33:38,708
She wanted to make sure she didn’t make any mistakes.

436
00:33:40,845 --> 00:33:43,428
Well, at least she didn’t take anything.

437
00:33:45,782 --> 00:33:48,049
This means Fah knew all along she had a twin.

438
00:33:48,346 --> 00:33:52,160
And after watching Sky for a while,
she learned how Sky dresses.

439
00:33:52,419 --> 00:33:53,440
And how she speaks.

440
00:33:54,335 --> 00:33:58,520
Or maybe Fah saw Sky on the news
when she was arrested or kidnapped.

441
00:33:59,405 --> 00:34:00,270
I don't think so.

442
00:34:00,620 --> 00:34:02,213
What do you mean, Doctor?

443
00:34:04,407 --> 00:34:06,582
Fah probably knew about Sky long before that.

444
00:34:07,729 --> 00:34:12,480
Remember how the first four bodies always used Morse code? But after we met Sky.

445
00:34:12,975 --> 00:34:16,840
The code changed each time,
until the fifth victim when Fah insulted us.

446
00:34:19,763 --> 00:34:21,043
What did it say, Sky?

447
00:34:22,091 --> 00:34:22,937
Morons.

448
00:34:24,068 --> 00:34:26,022
Morons need help from a retard kid.

449
00:34:26,518 --> 00:34:28,940
Morons need help from a retard kid.

450
00:34:29,257 --> 00:34:30,220
And ever since then

451
00:34:30,716 --> 00:34:33,512
Fah has always used Sky as a tool to communicate with us.

452
00:34:40,956 --> 00:34:43,561
Yes, I used her as my medium.

453
00:34:44,129 --> 00:34:46,068
And I'm the one who got her arrested.

454
00:34:46,960 --> 00:34:48,360
How exactly did you get her arrested?

455
00:35:42,760 --> 00:35:45,619
Huh? Did you deliberately frame your twin?

456
00:35:46,114 --> 00:35:49,272
No. I told you
I'm just using her as my medium.

457
00:35:49,600 --> 00:35:51,691
I want that cop to know the truth.

458
00:35:52,339 --> 00:35:57,916
And I'm sure he’ll never let my twin go to jail.

459
00:35:58,460 --> 00:36:01,139
Then what makes you so sure she'll be safe?

460
00:36:02,600 --> 00:36:04,712
Because that cop likes my twin.

461
00:36:14,891 --> 00:36:17,390
Fah never wanted Sky to take the blame.

462
00:36:18,480 --> 00:36:19,801
But it almost happened anyway.

463
00:36:22,982 --> 00:36:23,645
Yeah.

464
00:36:29,710 --> 00:36:32,167
Uh, almost what?

465
00:36:32,731 --> 00:36:33,580
Let's say, Sergeant

466
00:36:34,041 --> 00:36:36,659
If you wanted me to take the blame for you.

467
00:36:37,417 --> 00:36:40,300
What would you do before the trial?

468
00:36:41,462 --> 00:36:44,986
I'd probably lay low.

469
00:36:45,130 --> 00:36:45,752
Exactly.

470
00:36:45,830 --> 00:36:47,676
But Fah decided to kill her next victim.

471
00:36:48,045 --> 00:36:49,855
Just one day before the trial.

472
00:36:50,613 --> 00:36:53,455
That's why Sky was granted bail.

473
00:36:54,163 --> 00:36:54,960
I get it now.

474
00:36:56,750 --> 00:36:58,841
Fah is truly ruthless.

475
00:37:00,571 --> 00:37:01,680
Why would she go that far?

476
00:37:02,533 --> 00:37:06,114
At first, I didn't know
but once I found out Sky had a twin.

477
00:37:06,228 --> 00:37:10,087
I realized Fah wanted us to closely follow Sky's life.

478
00:37:10,441 --> 00:37:12,727
Until it led us to uncover the forged killer genes.

479
00:37:13,535 --> 00:37:14,099
Is this the reason why

480
00:37:14,312 --> 00:37:16,883
Lan asked us to check every victim's genes again.

481
00:37:17,386 --> 00:37:19,013
Fah wanted us to take a closer look at this.

482
00:37:19,561 --> 00:37:21,531
And that day when Fah broke
into the National Police Office

483
00:37:21,847 --> 00:37:23,287
She wanted those documents.

484
00:37:23,611 --> 00:37:25,779
I don't understand what the killer actually wants.

485
00:37:26,491 --> 00:37:28,011
Why does it have to be this complicated?

486
00:37:38,735 --> 00:37:42,840
After multiple failed attempts
by police to capture the Yarn Killer

487
00:37:43,123 --> 00:37:44,320
Recently, an anonymous source

488
00:37:44,380 --> 00:37:48,118
leaked autopsy reports detailing
the killer gene status of each victim.

489
00:37:48,300 --> 00:37:51,276
The reports confirmed that 8 out of 9
victims possessed the killer gene.

490
00:37:51,333 --> 00:37:53,916
However, civil registry records
were found to have been falsified.

491
00:37:54,140 --> 00:37:59,352
Officials had accepted bribes to alter documents for individuals carrying the killer gene.

492
00:37:59,466 --> 00:38:02,380
This operation involved systematically purchasing genetic identities from poorer individuals without the killer gene.

493
00:38:02,552 --> 00:38:04,240
Authorities believe the corruption was highly organized.

494
00:38:20,140 --> 00:38:21,017
Hey Keng

495
00:38:22,041 --> 00:38:22,986
It's time.

496
00:38:23,771 --> 00:38:25,638
Let's stick to the plan.

497
00:38:34,068 --> 00:38:35,340
Just a little longer, mom.

498
00:38:36,760 --> 00:38:37,702
It's finally time.

499
00:38:38,674 --> 00:38:41,207
I'll let you handle him yourself.

500
00:38:54,920 --> 00:38:56,979
How could you let those documents leak?

501
00:38:58,121 --> 00:38:59,523
Do you realize how much damage you've caused me?

502
00:39:00,560 --> 00:39:03,516
Do you know why I want to become Prime Minister?

503
00:39:04,120 --> 00:39:05,238
Yes, dad. I know.

504
00:39:06,440 --> 00:39:08,380
You want to pass a law

505
00:39:09,580 --> 00:39:11,390
to allow abortions for children carrying the killer gene.

506
00:39:12,540 --> 00:39:13,440
Good. At least you remember.

507
00:39:14,205 --> 00:39:15,733
I'm not doing this for myself.

508
00:39:16,377 --> 00:39:19,180
I'm doing it for everyone's safety. Remember that.

509
00:39:23,085 --> 00:39:26,525
Just keep working, Sergeant.
What's our progress?

510
00:39:27,640 --> 00:39:30,308
We’re working on the riddle of Grandpa Som’s Treasure.

511
00:39:30,876 --> 00:39:32,320
But we still haven't found the answer.

512
00:39:43,240 --> 00:39:45,240
Fah only kills people who have the killer genes.

513
00:39:46,670 --> 00:39:47,622
Let's start from here.

514
00:39:48,651 --> 00:39:50,064
If we don't know the answer yet, that's fine.

515
00:39:51,560 --> 00:39:55,729
Then let’s try connecting the answers
we already have back to the riddle.

516
00:39:57,580 --> 00:40:00,228
And I want the list of people
involved in forging the genes

517
00:40:00,327 --> 00:40:01,561
the one Mr Pakin gave us.
Where is it?

518
00:40:01,961 --> 00:40:03,070
Just a moment.

519
00:40:23,927 --> 00:40:25,234
That's all we have.

520
00:40:25,779 --> 00:40:27,127
Alright, let's start looking.

521
00:40:28,156 --> 00:40:29,333
If you're unsure about anything, say so first.

522
00:40:29,447 --> 00:40:30,472
I'll decide from there.

523
00:40:30,624 --> 00:40:31,367
Yes, Inspector.

524
00:40:37,310 --> 00:40:40,015
Let's see... the bank employees?

525
00:40:42,720 --> 00:40:44,632
Fah killed a bank employee before.

526
00:40:45,750 --> 00:40:47,310
I don’t think that's it, but

527
00:40:48,533 --> 00:40:49,481
separate them into another pile just in case.

528
00:40:49,577 --> 00:40:50,840
Make a special pile for the bank employees.

529
00:40:51,720 --> 00:40:52,998
Mr. Teeranai

530
00:40:53,531 --> 00:40:54,624
Sakuntamas

531
00:40:55,729 --> 00:40:57,078
Occupation: curator

532
00:40:57,942 --> 00:40:58,727
Huh?

533
00:40:59,409 --> 00:41:01,142
A curator the officer in charge of museums.

534
00:41:01,634 --> 00:41:02,590
Oh.

535
00:41:03,253 --> 00:41:05,561
Ah, alright, I get it now.

536
00:41:07,371 --> 00:41:08,160
That's an exact match.

537
00:41:10,849 --> 00:41:11,782
And what about this person?

538
00:41:12,727 --> 00:41:14,438
Ms. Jittima Riewpairoj.

539
00:41:14,617 --> 00:41:16,053
Librarian

540
00:41:20,876 --> 00:41:22,129
A librarian...

541
00:41:23,801 --> 00:41:24,520
Possible.

542
00:41:46,499 --> 00:41:47,360
Sergeant.

543
00:41:48,491 --> 00:41:49,320
Set this aside.

544
00:41:57,977 --> 00:42:00,167
These three people might be the answer to the riddle of Grandpa Som’s Treasure,

545
00:42:00,586 --> 00:42:02,198
and possibly the next victims.

546
00:42:04,460 --> 00:42:06,925
Mr. Teeranai, occuption: Curator

547
00:42:08,491 --> 00:42:11,546
Ms. Jittima, Occupation: Librarian

548
00:42:13,253 --> 00:42:14,171
Chanyanin

549
00:42:14,605 --> 00:42:16,000
Occupation: Antique shop owner

550
00:42:16,834 --> 00:42:17,321
Inspector

551
00:42:18,057 --> 00:42:19,348
Where did you get these three names?

552
00:42:19,641 --> 00:42:20,464
From Mr Pakin.

553
00:42:21,253 --> 00:42:24,350
Lieutenant, I want you to assign someone to tail these three.

554
00:42:24,680 --> 00:42:26,144
- Understood.
- But let me make this clear

555
00:42:26,666 --> 00:42:27,813
They must not suspect a thing.

556
00:42:28,571 --> 00:42:30,160
I want to use them as bait to lure the killer out.

557
00:42:30,483 --> 00:42:32,716
Got it. I’ll send someone right away.

558
00:42:41,497 --> 00:42:42,765
The cops are tailing them now.

559
00:42:43,550 --> 00:42:45,580
Good thing I noticed in time

560
00:42:45,881 --> 00:42:48,156
would’ve been screwed.
You idiots are starting to catch up, huh?

561
00:42:48,560 --> 00:42:51,348
Don’t think you’re the only smart one, Fah.

562
00:42:51,878 --> 00:42:54,080
There are plenty of people smarter
and sharper than you in this world.

563
00:42:55,520 --> 00:42:57,215
There’s always a higher sky above you, you know.

564
00:43:00,053 --> 00:43:01,024
I think it’s time you stopped.

565
00:43:01,763 --> 00:43:03,996
Your plan won’t work.
I’m not stopping.

566
00:43:05,855 --> 00:43:07,866
I’ll make it happen—no matter what.

567
00:43:09,530 --> 00:43:10,704
So what’s your next move?

568
00:43:13,000 --> 00:43:14,099
If they catch up to me

569
00:43:15,790 --> 00:43:17,607
I’ll do something they’d never expect.

570
00:43:18,720 --> 00:43:19,504
Like what?

571
00:43:27,649 --> 00:43:28,998
You go get this person for me instead.

572
00:43:31,640 --> 00:43:32,514
Are you serious?

573
00:43:33,089 --> 00:43:33,920
Yeah. It's time.

574
00:43:34,720 --> 00:43:35,542
Don’t you think so?

575
00:44:33,493 --> 00:44:34,320
This one’s yours.

576
00:44:35,234 --> 00:44:36,182
Now get the hell out of here.

577
00:44:38,708 --> 00:44:39,580
This time, I don’t want any money.

578
00:44:41,356 --> 00:44:43,180
Just make sure you clear this bastard’s debt for me instead.

579
00:44:43,939 --> 00:44:45,215
You’ll get your payback.

580
00:45:29,843 --> 00:45:31,131
Officer.

581
00:45:31,672 --> 00:45:34,986
Are you staying at Sky’s house again tonight?

582
00:45:36,464 --> 00:45:37,280
Yes

583
00:45:37,977 --> 00:45:39,219
Is Sky okay?

584
00:45:41,767 --> 00:45:43,127
Sky's okay.

585
00:45:43,641 --> 00:45:46,537
But why don’t you just sleep at your own place?

586
00:45:46,918 --> 00:45:50,979
Don’t your parents mind you sleeping
at Sky’s house every night like this?

587
00:45:52,259 --> 00:45:53,219
Sky

588
00:45:54,011 --> 00:45:55,714
Enough now, Sky

589
00:46:00,236 --> 00:46:02,152
And Sky, time to get ready for bed.

590
00:46:02,784 --> 00:46:04,260
This is for you, Officer.

591
00:46:04,815 --> 00:46:06,179
- Thank you, Miss Sookwan
- You're welcome.

592
00:46:28,920 --> 00:46:32,240
- Must die... must die...
- Sky! What’s wrong, Sky?

593
00:46:32,520 --> 00:46:33,800
- Sky... Sky...
- Sky must go.

594
00:46:33,916 --> 00:46:35,744
- Officer, what’s happening to Sky?
- Miss Sookwan. Miss Sookwan

595
00:46:35,900 --> 00:46:37,116
- Let Sky go.
- Sky must go.

596
00:46:37,160 --> 00:46:39,120
- Can I come with you?
- Don't worry. I’ll take care of her.

597
00:46:44,240 --> 00:46:46,280
- Must die...
- I’ll go after her myself.

598
00:48:05,520 --> 00:48:06,360
Let me go, you psycho!

599
00:48:11,980 --> 00:48:12,840
Oh, you’re awake?

600
00:48:15,640 --> 00:48:16,600
Let me go, bitch!

601
00:48:18,800 --> 00:48:19,927
I heard you were trying to run.

602
00:48:26,840 --> 00:48:29,120
I’ll make sure you disappear for good.

603
00:48:45,005 --> 00:48:46,457
Woah, you know how to stop bleeding too?

604
00:48:47,120 --> 00:48:48,160
Impressive.

605
00:48:54,179 --> 00:48:55,040
What? You scared now?

606
00:48:56,883 --> 00:48:57,992
Now you’re scared.

607
00:49:02,050 --> 00:49:03,714
But when you were selling our genes

608
00:49:05,032 --> 00:49:05,859
you weren’t scared then, were you?

609
00:51:56,880 --> 00:51:58,720
Sky must go. Sky must go.

610
00:51:59,680 --> 00:52:01,480
Die. Die.

611
00:52:02,920 --> 00:52:04,720
Must go. Must die.

612
00:52:06,520 --> 00:52:09,520
Sky must go. Must die. Must die.

613
00:52:20,480 --> 00:52:23,080
Must go. Must die.

614
00:52:23,560 --> 00:52:25,080
Must die. Must die.
